{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LOOP ITERATION 7 — STORY SPLIT. Review round 8 returned 11 blocks (round 7 had 14). Two double-digit\nrounds is not convergence, and reading them showed WHY: most were self-contradictions bred by one plan\ncarrying two concerns.\n\nThe clearest example, flagged three separate ways by round 8: my Approach said 'translate at the\nadapter into the neutral types the core ALREADY handles' — which implies no core edits — while my\nScope listed dispatch_apply_phases.py and outbound_differ.py as modified, and an AC implied core catch\nclauses change. All three cannot be true. That tension was structural, not a wording slip, so no\namount of rewording was going to settle it.\n\nSPLIT: the exception contract is now [rebar:bb8c-8283-80c6-4052] (J10), which BLOCKS this story. J10\nis small and self-contained — declare BackendHTTPError on the port SUBCLASSING urllib.error.HTTPError,\ntranslate JIRAError in the DC transport. The subclass choice is what makes the contradiction vanish:\ncore catch clauses need NO change (a subclass matches the existing except), and Cloud is untouched,\nwhich the brainstorm's decision 7 requires ('must not alter or replace the live-validated Cloud path').\n\nALSO FIXED HERE, from round 8's remaining real findings:\n * _identity_of's KEY is now SPECIFIED, not left open. The existing account_id key receives\n   'accountId or name'. Round 8 correctly noted the idempotence AC depends on WHICH key, and I had\n   only said 'carry the name'. Measured across all three shapes: {accountId}->'557058:abc' (Cloud\n   unchanged), {name}->'dcuser' (DC fixed), {accountId,name}->'557058:abc' (accountId wins, Cloud does\n   not regress). The priority is load-bearing and a test must pin it.\n * outbound_field_diff.py is now explicitly documented as NOT a patch site, with the reason — it has\n   been flagged three times. Once _identity_of populates account_id, _diff_reporter's comparison\n   converges with no edit. It is a DIFFERENT FILE from outbound_differ.py, which is J10's concern; the\n   near-identical names are a genuine trap.\n\nadd_issue_property, disputed for a THIRD round, is now settled by three independent methods and the\nplan cites all three: grep of the installed file gives 'def add_issue_property' at LINE 2961 of\n.venv/lib/python3.14/site-packages/jira/client.py; inspect.signature agrees; pip show confirms 3.10.5.\nThe method is wrapped in @translate_resource_args, which is why a STATIC resolver keeps missing it.\n\nSEQUENCING CONSEQUENCE, worth stating because it inverts the obvious order: J9 is now BLOCKED by J10,\nand review-plan FAST-FAILS on a ticket blocked by an unclosed dependency. So J10 is reviewed, landed\nand closed FIRST; only then does J9 become reviewable. Reviewing J9 now would fail with no LLM spent."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785487519609038001,"uuid":"50f556b7-7121-42a1-810b-7e7df26f7e28"}